# ── Secrets ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*-service-account.json

# ── Python ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.venv/
venv/
build/
dist/

# ── Test and tooling artefacts ───────────────────────────────────────────────
.pytest_cache/
.pytest-*.xml
.pytest-*.log
.coverage
htmlcov/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/

# ── Runtime data ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Evidence is CCTV imagery of identifiable people. It must never enter version
# control, where deletion does not delete.
data/
media/
crops/
logs/

# ── Models ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# v1 is the only model (since 2026-10-22), committed deliberately: the
# deployment must be reproducible from a checkout. Two exports of the same
# fine-tuned v1.pt, which stays local:
#   v1-640.onnx  the PERSON DETECTOR (640 input; narrowed to `person` by
#                VISION_DETECTOR_CLASSES). 9.8 MB.
#   v1.onnx      the 'region_head' understander's PPE answers (hairnet, glove,
#                mask, apron and their absences) on 448 crops. 9.7 MB.
# yolo11s / yolov8n / yolov8n-pose were removed; they are in git history.
# Everything else under models/ is an experiment.
models/*
!models/v1-640.onnx
!models/v1.onnx

# ── Production datasets ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# P9.7. `datasets/` held 723 MB of CCTV-derived frames of identifiable people
# with no ignore rule at all: a single `git add .` would have published them to
# GitHub, where deletion does not delete.
#
# The corpus now lives OUTSIDE the repository, under $VISION_OS_DATA_ROOT. What
# stays here is the small, reviewable record that makes an experiment
# reproducible — manifests, schemas, reports — and never the pixels.
#
# Ignore the pixels wherever they appear...
datasets/**/*.jpg
datasets/**/*.jpeg
datasets/**/*.png
datasets/**/*.bmp
datasets/**/*.tif
datasets/**/*.tiff
datasets/**/*.webp
datasets/**/*.mp4
datasets/**/*.avi
datasets/**/*.mkv
datasets/**/*.mov
datasets/**/*.webm

# Deliberately NOT excluding the collection directories wholesale. Git cannot
# re-include a file whose parent directory is excluded, so a `datasets/p9-live/`
# rule would also swallow session.json, quality.json and review_queue.json —
# precisely the metadata that makes a collection reproducible and citable.
# Measured during P9.7: it did exactly that.
#
# The extension rules above already catch every pixel. What remains — manifests,
# digests, boxes, counts, provenance, reports — identifies nobody and belongs in
# version control with the code that used it.
